+With `prompt_cut` (class knob, default 0) waiting prompt work (S4.8) that
+is due also stops an item of another queue at its next such point: a
+4 KiB read need not wait out a 1 MiB write.  Such an item keeps its turn:
+its queue goes to the ring's head with what is left of its deficit, runs
+next after the prompt work and before anything new, and gets no refill
+when taken, nor does that count as a ring slot for S4.8, so the prompt
+bound still holds.  Without this it would go to the ring's tail, and each
+read would leave another item part done, which is what `item_min_us` is
+there to avoid.  `keep_turn` (class knob, default 0) keeps the turn of an
+item stopped for a higher class in the same way.
+
